---
import MadhouseLayout from '../../../layouts/MadhouseLayout.astro';
---

<MadhouseLayout
	variant="legal"
	seo={{
		title: 'Privacy Policy – Madhouse Darts App',
		description:
			'Privacy Policy of the Madhouse darts scoring app: what data is processed through Firebase Analytics and Firebase Crashlytics, how it is used and what rights you have.',
	}}
>
	<main id="content" class="mh-legal">
		<article class="mh-legal__article">
			<div class="mh-legal__head" data-intro>
				<p class="mh-eyebrow">Legal</p>
				<h1 class="mh-legal__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
				<p class="mh-legal__meta">Effective date: <strong>25.10.2026</strong></p>
			</div>
			<p class="mh-legal__intro">
				<strong>Madhouse</strong> respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information is processed when
				you use the Madhouse app on iPhone, iPad and Android, why it is processed, and which rights you have.
			</p>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Who Is Responsible</h2>
				<p>The controller responsible for processing your personal data under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:</p>
				<p>Niko Börger<br />Gottfried-Keller-Straße 9<br />22848 Norderstedt<br />Germany</p>
				<p>Email: <span data-mail>[Please enable Javascript]</span></p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Data Stored on Your Device</h2>
				<p>
					Your players, matches, statistics and settings are stored <strong>only on your device</strong>. Madhouse has
					no user accounts and no server of its own, so this data is never uploaded to us.
				</p>
				<p>
					If you add a picture to a player, the app asks for access to your camera or photo library. The picture you
					take or choose is stored only on your device. You can remove it at any time, and all app data is deleted when
					you uninstall the app.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Information We Collect</h2>
				<p>
					We use <strong>Firebase Analytics</strong>, a service provided by Google, to understand how our app is used
					and to improve its performance and features. Firebase Analytics automatically collects certain information,
					which may include:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Device information (e.g., model, operating system version, language)</li>
					<li>App usage data (e.g., screens viewed, sessions, app version)</li>
					<li>General location information (e.g., country, region), derived from your IP address</li>
					<li>Online identifiers such as a randomly generated app instance ID and, where available, your device's advertising identifier</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					We also use <strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong>, a service provided by Google, to find and fix crashes. If
					the app crashes or runs into a serious error, a crash report is sent. It contains technical information such
					as the error details, device model, operating system and app version, the state of the device at the time of
					the crash, and a randomly generated installation ID.
				</p>
				<p>
					We <strong>do not</strong> collect personally identifiable information such as your name, email address,
					phone number, or precise location. Madhouse shows no ads and does not track you across other apps or
					websites.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>How We Use the Information</h2>
				<p>The information collected through Firebase Analytics and Firebase Crashlytics is used solely for:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Monitoring app performance and stability</li>
					<li>Finding and fixing crashes and errors</li>
					<li>Improving the user experience</li>
					<li>Understanding how users interact with the app</li>
				</ul>
				<p>We do not sell or share your data with third parties for marketing or advertising purposes.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Legal Basis</h2>
				<p>
					We process this data on the basis of our legitimate interest in providing a stable, error free app and in
					improving it (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
				<p>
					Our app uses Firebase Analytics and Firebase Crashlytics, which are provided by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon
					House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland, and Google LLC. For details about how Google handles data in
					Firebase, please refer to Google's privacy documentation:
				</p>
				<p>
					<a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google - Privacy &amp; Security in Firebase →</a>
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>International Data Transfers</h2>
				<p>
					Google may process data in the United States and other countries outside the European Economic Area. These
					transfers are based on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, under which Google LLC is certified, and on the
					European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Data Retention</h2>
				<p>
					Analytics data is retained by Firebase according to Google's retention settings. Crashlytics keeps crash
					reports and the associated identifiers for 90 days. We do not store this data ourselves.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Your Choices</h2>
				<p>
					You can object to the processing at any time by contacting us. On Android, you can reset your advertising ID
					or delete it in your device settings under Google, then Ads. On iOS, you can manage tracking under Settings,
					then Privacy &amp; Security, then Tracking. Uninstalling the app stops all data collection.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Your Rights</h2>
				<p>Under the GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>access your personal data (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
					<li>have it corrected (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
					<li>have it deleted (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
					<li>restrict its processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
					<li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
					<li>object to its processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority. The authority
					responsible for us is the Unabhängiges Landeszentrum für Datenschutz Schleswig-Holstein (ULD), but you may
					also contact the authority in your country of residence.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
				<p>
					Madhouse is a general audience app and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal data
					from children.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The current version is always available on this page,
					and the effective date above shows when it was last changed.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="mh-legal__section" data-reveal>
				<h2>Contact Us</h2>
				<p>
					If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:
					<span data-mail class="mh-mail--strong">[Please enable Javascript]</span>
				</p>
			</section>
		</article>
	</main>
</MadhouseLayout>
